 "transcript": {
  "answer": "Yes. Eating out in Melbourne is getting more expensive, but prices are rising a little more slowly than the overall CPI.\n\n**Latest figures (August 2026, ABS monthly CPI)**\n- Meals out and takeaway prices in Melbourne were **3.5% higher** than in August 2025.\n- Melbourne's overall CPI was also up **3.5%** over the same period, so restaurant and takeaway prices are now rising at about the same pace as everything else.\n\n**Recent trend**\n- Annual inflation for meals out was **2.6%** in April 2025.\n- It reached **4.4%** in May 2026, which is the recent peak.\n- It then eased to 3.9% in June, 4.1% in July and 3.5% in August 2026.\n- Meals out have risen by more than 3% a year in every month since August 2025.\n\n**Longer view**\n- The ABS quarterly index for meals out and takeaway in Melbourne rose from 124.3 in September 2021 to 150.4 in September 2025. That is about **21% in four years**.\n- The biggest jump was in 2022 and 2023, when annual price growth was much faster than it has been recently.\n\nThe index levels before and after September 2025 use different bases, so I haven't joined them into one figure.",
